-- ClassLess: the whole tome loot table, emitted from the GROUP rule.
--
-- GENERATED by tools/classless-web/emit_groups.py -- regenerate, do not hand-edit.
--
-- An ability belongs to a group (who fights like that, which five levels); a creature
-- belongs to the groups its own kind answers for. So the world data is two tables:
--
--   reference_loot_template  one per group, holding that band's abilities by weight.
--                            The weights of a table sum to 100, so a roll into it always
--                            returns exactly one ability.
--   creature_loot_template   one row per creature per group: Item 0, Reference <table>,
--                            Chance = how often that creature gives a tome at all.
--
-- Rare pre-cast buffs are the exception: boss-only by rule, so they are plain item rows on
-- the shallowest bosses that may hold them.
--
-- This file REPLACES classless_tome_loot.sql and the per-row placement it came from.

-- Our reference band, and every tome row anywhere, so no earlier placement can survive.
DELETE FROM `reference_loot_template` WHERE `Entry` BETWEEN 1900000 AND 1900999;
DELETE FROM `creature_loot_template` WHERE `Reference` BETWEEN 1900000 AND 1900999;
DELETE FROM `creature_loot_template` WHERE `Item` BETWEEN 63000 AND 66999;

-- The group tables. GroupId 1 makes each one a pick-one; the chances are relative and
-- sum to 100 per table, so entering a table always yields an ability.

-- Every carrier below loots from a table named by its own entry. Asserted
-- unconditionally, including where it is already true: a creature at lootid 0 has no
-- loot table at all, so without this its rows exist and are never read.
